From a4d8536b0957d5f8298225b8074a707eada5757f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ocd0711 <ocd2057try@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Jan 2026 10:21:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher3: Add support for 2x2 expandable large folder in
 workspace

This change adds support for expandable large folders in the workspace.

A large folder occupies a 2x2 cell when expanded and displays a 3x3 grid of app icons. Icons inside the folder can be interacted with directly, supporting both click-to-launch and long-press operations, without needing to open the folder first.

Known limitations:
1. Some comments in the modified code are still written in Chinese and will be converted to English in a follow-up change.
2. When large folders are enabled, workspace icons are currently centered vertically. Due to the lack of a reliable method to calculate the top margin, the CenterVertically parameter is temporarily not applied.

Note:
Some animations are designed for the 3x3 folder preview layout, and the original 2x2 layout in Launcher3 has not been modified yet. Layout adjustments for the 2x2 grid will be addressed in future updates.

Change-Id: I2211e5982463bd6989042515c57023bfb3c8ba83
